senses.gloss:
अभि॑ adv. to, unto, near (comp. अभितर॑म् or ˚रा॑म्
nearer);
 towards, against;
 as prep. the same + into, for, for the sake
of, over, above, concerning, about (acc.);
 without, except (abl.).

अभी॑क n. encountering, meeting;
 loc. at the same time or
in time;
 out of or from out (abl.).

अभिकाम a. affectionate, loving, desirous of (acc. or
—˚);
 m. affection, love, desire.

अभिख्या॑ f. sight, glance (subj. & obj), brightness,
clearness, splendour, glory beauty;
 name, designation.

अभि॑तस् adv. & prep. (w. acc.) towards, near;
 around,
behind, before and after.

अभिधान n. = prec. f. + statement, speech, discourse,
word;
 also = seq;
 f. ˚धा॑नी a halter.

अभिधेय a. to be named or expressed;
 n. meaning,
signification.

अभिनव a. quite new or fresh;
 अभिनव++˚यौवन &
अभिनव˚वयस्क a. of tender youth, very young.

अभिनीत a. brought near, adduced, performed;
 trained,
educated;
 fit, proper.

अभिप्राय m. intention, purpose, goal, object, wish,
opinion, meaning;
 the conception (of a thing) as (—˚).

अभिमान m. = prec. abstr.;
 self-conceit, arrogance,
pride (p. ˚वन्त्);
 affection, love;
 conception, supposition, esp. a
false one.

अभिमानिन् a. self-conceited, arrogant;
 imagining one's
self to have or to be (—˚).

अभिमुख f. ई (आ) having the face towards, facing,
turned to (acc., dat., gen., or —˚);
 propitious, favourable to (gen. or
instr.);
 approaching, near;
 occupied in, going to (—˚). n. adv. in
front, towards, against, over against (acc., gen. or —˚);
 ˚खे
against, opposite (gen. or —˚). ˚खी भू turn towards, be favourable.

अभियुक्त a. assailed, charged, prosecuted (j);
 intent
on (loc. or —˚), versed in (loc.), competent.

अभियोग m. application, endeavour, effort at (loc. or
—˚);
 attack, assault, accusation.

अभिराम a. agreeable, pleasing;
 m. = seq.;
 abstr. ˚ता
f., (˚त्व n.*).

अभिवादन n. = prec. m.;
 ˚शील a. respectful,
modest.

अभिव्याहृत a. spoken to;
 said, uttered;
 n. word.

अभि॑शस्ति f. imprecation, curse;
 censure, blame;
misfortune, harm;
 concr. a slanderer, enemy.

अभिषङ्ग m. inclination, attachment, curse,
imprecation;
 defeat, humiliation;
 a. ˚न्गिन् defeating, humiliating.

अभिषेक॑ m. sprinkling over, bathing, religious,
ablation, consecration, inauguration;
 the consecrated water itself.

अभिषेचनी॑य a. worthy or destined to be
consecrated;
 m. consecration.

अभिसंहित a. directed, turned;
 intended, agreed;
connected with (—˚).

अभिसंधान n. holding together, union;
 declaration,
statement, speech;
 aim, purpose, interest;
 cheating, deceiving.

अभिसृत a. come, gone to (acc.) or against (—˚);
 turned
towards (—˚);
 visited by (instr.).

अभि॑हित a. fastened, attached;
 yoked;
 said, spoken
named, designated, declared, addressed, called.

अभी॑ष्ट a. longed for, wished, pleasant, dear. m.
favourite, lover;
 n. wish.

आभिमुख्य n. direction towards (gen., acc., or —˚),
intention to (—˚);
 ˚करण n. calling hither.
